 "assignments": [
  {
   "id": "a_m13_psr",
   "title": "Primary Source Report: Kennedy or Johnson",
   "html": "<div id=\"sparkled-assessment\"><div style=\"background:#0F2330; border-bottom:4px solid #0A6C94; border-radius:10px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:20px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px; color:#F4D35E; margin-bottom:6px;\"><strong>MODULE PROJECT</strong></div><div style=\"font-family:'Rokkitt',Rockwell,Georgia,serif; font-size:26px; color:#FFFFFF; line-height:1.25; margin-bottom:6px;\">Primary Source Report: Kennedy or Johnson</div><div style=\"font-size:15px; color:#DCEEF6;\">20 points · Word document · one turn-in</div></div><div style=\"border-top:3px double #0A6C94; margin:0 0 20px;\"></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #0F2330; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#0F2330; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Your task</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\">This week you read two sources: President Kennedy's address on missiles in Cuba, and President Johnson's address at the University of Michigan. Choose <strong>one</strong> of them and write a report of about 400 to 500 words that evaluates it as a historian would.</p></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #0A6C94; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#0A6C94; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Your Five Steps</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\">Your report should do five things, in this order:</p><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px; overflow:hidden;\"><div style=\"float:left; width:28px; height:28px; line-height:28px; text-align:center; border-radius:50%; background:#0F2330; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:15px; margin-right:12px;\">1</div><div style=\"margin-left:42px; font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Place the source.</strong> Who spoke, when, and to whom? What was the speaker trying to get listeners to do or believe?</div></div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px; overflow:hidden;\"><div style=\"float:left; width:28px; height:28px; line-height:28px; text-align:center; border-radius:50%; background:#0F2330; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:15px; margin-right:12px;\">2</div><div style=\"margin-left:42px; font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6;\"><strong>State the main claim</strong> in your own words.</div></div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px; overflow:hidden;\"><div style=\"float:left; width:28px; height:28px; line-height:28px; text-align:center; border-radius:50%; background:#0F2330; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:15px; margin-right:12px;\">3</div><div style=\"margin-left:42px; font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Point to evidence.</strong> Quote or describe one specific passage the speaker uses to support the claim.</div></div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px; overflow:hidden;\"><div style=\"float:left; width:28px; height:28px; line-height:28px; text-align:center; border-radius:50%; background:#0F2330; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:15px; margin-right:12px;\">4</div><div style=\"margin-left:42px; font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Test the claim.</strong> Using the lesson \"Kennedy: Berlin, Cuba, and the Brink\" or the source John F. Kennedy, Address on Missiles in Cuba, say what the lesson confirms, what it complicates, and what the speaker leaves out.</div></div><div style=\"margin:0 0 12px; overflow:hidden;\"><div style=\"float:left; width:28px; height:28px; line-height:28px; text-align:center; border-radius:50%; background:#0F2330; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:15px; margin-right:12px;\">5</div><div style=\"margin-left:42px; font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Name a limit.</strong> Tell one thing you cannot learn about this period from this source alone.</div></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\">Write in complete paragraphs. You do not need a title page. Cite the source and the lesson by name.</p></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #B02A24; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#B02A24; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Before you submit</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\"><strong>Before you submit:</strong></p><ul style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px; padding-left:26px;\"><li style=\"margin-bottom:8px;\">Write your report in Word and save it to your course folder in OneDrive.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:8px;\">Name your file: LastName_FirstName_PrimarySourceReport5_HIS10</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:8px;\">Submit through Canvas using the OneDrive tab or a file upload.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:8px;\">Need help? Open the \"M365 Setup &amp; File Organization Guide\" linked in this module.</li></ul></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #0F2330; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#0F2330; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Rubric</strong></div><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; margin-top:6px;\"><tbody><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; text-align:left; vertical-align:top; background:#DCEEF6; font-size:14px; width:22%;\">Understanding of the material<br><span style=\"color:#0A6C94;\">5.0 pts</span></th><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>5.0 pts</strong> Strong<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">Source and lesson used accurately; steps 1 to 4 all present</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>3.0 pts</strong> Developing<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">Mostly accurate; one step thin</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>1.0 pts</strong> Beginning<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">Source misread or lesson not used</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>0.0 pts</strong> No evidence<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\"></span></td></tr><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; text-align:left; vertical-align:top; background:#DCEEF6; font-size:14px; width:22%;\">Quality of reasoning<br><span style=\"color:#0A6C94;\">5.0 pts</span></th><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>5.0 pts</strong> Strong<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">Tests the claim against evidence and weighs both</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>3.0 pts</strong> Developing<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">Reports the claim, tests it lightly</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>1.0 pts</strong> Beginning<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">Summarizes only</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>0.0 pts</strong> No evidence<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\"></span></td></tr><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; text-align:left; vertical-align:top; background:#DCEEF6; font-size:14px; width:22%;\">Clarity and precision<br><span style=\"color:#0A6C94;\">5.0 pts</span></th><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>5.0 pts</strong> Strong<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">Organized in paragraphs, precise, within length</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>3.0 pts</strong> Developing<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">Understandable, some wandering</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>1.0 pts</strong> Beginning<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">Hard to follow or far off length</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>0.0 pts</strong> No evidence<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\"></span></td></tr><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; text-align:left; vertical-align:top; background:#DCEEF6; font-size:14px; width:22%;\">Intellectual honesty<br><span style=\"color:#0A6C94;\">5.0 pts</span></th><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>5.0 pts</strong> Strong<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">The limit in step 5 is real and specific</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>3.0 pts</strong> Developing<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">Limit is generic</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>1.0 pts</strong> Beginning<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">No limit named</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>0.0 pts</strong> No evidence<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\"></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>",
