 "discussions": [
  {
   "id": "d_m13",
   "title": "Discussion: Cuban Missile Crisis: Brinkmanship or Statesmanship?",
   "html": "<div id=\"sparkled-assessment\"><div style=\"background:#0F2330; border-bottom:4px solid #0A6C94; border-radius:10px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:20px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px; color:#F4D35E; margin-bottom:6px;\"><strong>DISCUSSION</strong></div><div style=\"font-family:'Rokkitt',Rockwell,Georgia,serif; font-size:26px; color:#FFFFFF; line-height:1.25; margin-bottom:6px;\">Discussion: Cuban Missile Crisis: Brinkmanship or Statesmanship?</div><div style=\"font-size:15px; color:#DCEEF6;\">10 points · threaded discussion</div></div><div style=\"border-top:3px double #0A6C94; margin:0 0 20px;\"></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #B02A24; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#B02A24; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Before you start</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\">Open the lesson \"Kennedy: Berlin, Cuba, and the Brink\". Use My Notebook on that page to gather your notes and marks, then come back here to post.</p></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #0F2330; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#0F2330; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>The question</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\">For thirteen days in October 1962, the world came close to nuclear war. Critics say President Kennedy gambled with the world over missiles that did not change the balance of power. Defenders say he showed the judgment of a skilled statesman. Was it brinkmanship or statesmanship?</p></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #0A6C94; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#0A6C94; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Your post</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\"><strong>Your post (about 100 to 150 words):</strong></p><ol style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 6px; padding-left:22px;\"><li style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">Take a clear position: brinkmanship, statesmanship, or a mix that leans one way.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">Give one specific piece of evidence from the lesson \"Kennedy: Berlin, Cuba, and the Brink\" that supports you.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\">Name one fact that cuts against your position, and explain why you still hold it.</li></ol></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #B02A24; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#B02A24; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Your reply</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\"><strong>Your reply (about 50 to 75 words):</strong> Respond to one classmate. Do you agree with their reasoning? If so, strengthen it with something they did not use. If not, say respectfully where their reasoning falls short.</p></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #0F2330; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#0F2330; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Before you post</strong></div><p style=\"font-size:17px; color:#1C1B1A; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 10px;\">Post first, then reply. You will not see your classmates' posts until you have posted.</p></div><div style=\"background:#FFFDF8; border:1px solid #DCD4C4; border-top:4px solid #0F2330; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 22px; margin-bottom:18px;\"><div style=\"display:inline-block; background:#0F2330; color:#FFFFFF; font-size:12px; padding:4px 10px; border-radius:999px; margin-bottom:12px;\"><strong>Rubric</strong></div><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; margin-top:6px;\"><tbody><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; text-align:left; vertical-align:top; background:#DCEEF6; font-size:14px; width:22%;\">Post and reply<br><span style=\"color:#0A6C94;\">10.0 pts</span></th><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>10.0 pts</strong> Substantive<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">Clear position, specific evidence from the week, names a counterpoint, and the reply engages a classmate's actual reasoning</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>6.0 pts</strong> Thin<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">Position stated but evidence vague, no counterpoint, or the reply only says \"I agree\"</span></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #DCD4C4; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; font-size:14px;\"><strong>0.0 pts</strong> Missing<br><span style=\"color:#55524C;\">No post, or no reply</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>",
